{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/632408-convention-bastet-s-beloved-the-kitten-cuddlers","id":632408,"title":"Convention: Bastet's Beloved, The Kitten Cuddlers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-19T09:46:07-07:00","id":632408,"title":"Convention: Bastet's Beloved, The Kitten Cuddlers","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/yhnGSVV.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <div align=\"center\">Art by Reper Verse</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>\u201cHave you heard?\u201d Said Spot. \u201cTibbers saw a dead man watching the college where they throw out fish every Thursday.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut that\u2019s the anointed one\u2019s school\u201d replied Scrufmuffin in horror.<br /> <br /> Tigger\u2019s blood boiled in rage as he sniffed the latest news from a lamppost. \u201cCome! Smell this!\u201d he shouted loud enough to wake humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lugosi waited in a dusty attic. He was amusing himself by listening to the heartbeats of ignorant humans below and wondering which of the college girls across the street he\u2019d make into his brides when he heard a soft thump and a tiny heartbeat behind him. Then another and another. He turned and a dozen reflective eyes stared unblinking at him from the shadows.<br /> <br /> Something with the weight of a grown man landed directly on the Lugosi\u2019s shoulders knocking him off balance. Claws dug into his back and cut deep grooves into his ribs. The vampire rolled onto his back and sized a house cat and began to crush it between his hands.<br /> <br /> Two cats pounced in sequence, each shredding the muscles in an arm beneath their claws. Lugosi dropped the cat and began to shape the magic animating his body, forcing his arms to work without tendons when a cat leapt up and gouged out his eyes. The vampire stumbled backwards trying to track his assailants by their heartbeats, he picked a target and lunged by without supernatural speed the cat easily dived out the way. In mid stride a cat tackled Lugosi\u2019s knee with the weight of a grown man and sent him flying. The pride moved in for the kill.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness a god is more than just an all-powerful long bearded man in the sky. A god can include choirs of angels or entire worlds just as you include your little finger. A God can even include, be, or be the product of (if such distinctions apply to the divine) natural laws.<br /> <br /> One such Goddess is Bastet of the Netjer, whose worship dates back almost to 3000 BC. Revered throughout Ancient Egypt as a protector deity, Bastet gave her sacred cats to the nation. Her cats would patrol the land, protecting it\u2019s food supplies from vermin and protecting the people from cobras and worse threats.<br /> <br /> In modern nights\u2026 nothing much has changed. If Bastet smiles upon you, then the cats will keep you safe.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Enemy</span><br /> <br /> While the Goddess\u2019 invisible support helps her Beloved quickly come to terms with their ability to talk to cats, they are still citizens of the World of Darkness. Most have little knowledge of the supernatural and little interest in seeking out the occult in dark corners to fight it, or otherwise. Even if they did the Beloved have no institution to transmit policy about different foes.<br /> <br /> It is not Bastet\u2019s Beloved who have enemies, it is Bastet Herself, and Bastet\u2019s enemies are anyone who threaten her Beloved.<br /> <br /> Vampires need to feed upon humans and cats don\u2019t have the patience or the cultural knowledge to determine their feeding habits, if a vampire is in the area the claws come out. Beasts also prey on humanity and while a cat\u2019s knowledge of Ancient Egyptian theology is on the same level as an eight year old catholic\u2019s knowledge of christianity that\u2019s enough for them to point out, often lethally, that teaching humanity is the job of priests and gods, whose motives are purer and whose methods are less traumatic.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s not to say that cats have any supernatural ability to recognise vampires or beasts, or any culture of shared knowledge about them. Rather, once a cats see a vampire go for the throat in a dark alleyway they\u2019re quick to judge.<br /> <br /> Against more powerful enemies, particularly if they have a connection to the divine like Leviathans or Mummies, cats are quick to suggest asking a higher power for help. Unfortunately cats don\u2019t have international communication networks, today they don\u2019t know where to find Bastet\u2019s priesthood or if the priesthood still exists. Bastet\u2019s Beloved who don\u2019t realise that as the human they\u2019re supposed to be the intelligent and forward thinking one often end up on a flight to Egypt with no clue what they\u2019re going to do when they land.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hunters</span><br /> <br /> Not long ago the Vampire who claimed feeding rights over your neighbourhood vanished. Shortly afterwards the mismatched trio of newly embraced vampires sent to investigate vanished. Then so did the Prince\u2019s agent sent to do the job properly. Now all the vampires eyes turn towards your neighbourhood. You don\u2019t know this of course, you don\u2019t know vampires exist either, you\u2019re only nine years old.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re a witch. Not a particularly powerful witch but you have some tricks and a black cat. You never tried to attract Bastet\u2019s attention, in fact you always considered yourself more a Maiden, Mother, Crone sort of witch but when a goddess chooses you you know the only acceptable response is humble gratitude. New artwork and new theurgy textbooks it is. In truth Bastet isn\u2019t giving you much power beyond her Mantle, but you wouldn\u2019t dare be ungrateful.<br /> <br /> One day you can home and your boyfriend was different, scary. He insisted he loved you and only wanted to be together, but your cat saw the truth. When he was alone he walked through a door and on the other side he was a hulking man shaped bat. Together you\u2019re on the run, stealing to survive. It seems he won't ever let you go.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re a ranger in the safaris of Africa. You fight poachers and you love all the animals under your care, the lions most of all. You also have no idea why all sorts of weird people keep coming to you for advice or your blessing.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s no polite way to put it. You\u2019re a crazy cat lady. Unlike most of your contemporaries you\u2019re actually competent at caring for a house full of cats. Your guests are well fed and healthy, which is why Bastet loves you. Another thing sets you apart from your contemporaries, your craziness comes from spending all your life in the vicinity of a Mummy\u2019s tomb. The presence of a Goddess has help focused the oracular abilities inflicted by living in a Mummy\u2019s arua. With your army of cats you will chase the vermin from your town, you will prove Bastet and the civilisation of Egypt superior to the brutality of Irem\u2019s Judges and their scorpion cults.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Stereotypes</span><br /> <br /> The Union: Dad came home upset that people at the factory were gossiping about me and Tigger. I think they lost interest, he\u2019s much happier these days.<br /> <br /> Hakollel shel Hamerkava: Coca loves to point out flaws in the Torah. I asked the rabbi about some of Coca\u2019s ideas and he smiled and gave me a book full of big words, but I could tell he was upset when he spoke to mum and dad.<br /> <br /> The Athenic Church: Mr Biscuit says my cousin\u2019s friends will all end up old and lonely so I shouldn\u2019t be like them. My cousin says I need to spend less time playing with Mr Biscuit and more time doing my homework if I want to make a meaningful contribution to society.<br /> <br /> Null Mysteriis: My science teacher is really fun. He asks me to spend lunch wearing a funny hat and talking to his kittens, and he gives me sweets and answers for my homework if I don\u2019t tell anyone.<br /> <br /> <i>Picture: A young girl in a cutesy dress is hugging a kitten. On the wall behind them the cat has no shadow; instead you can see a shadow of a lioness grooming the girl\u2019s hair.<br /> <br /> I love my kitty witty!</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Status</span><br /> <br /> Bastet's Beloved shouldn't really have Status. There's no organization, no ladder to climb, heck. Most members could go their whole lives without meeting another. Yet there is something, when two of Bastet's Beloved meet they can both feel the mark of Bastet upon the other. It's an instinctive respect, closer to what one lion might feel for the pride's leader than human trust, but it's respect all the same.<br /> <br /> Because of this Status measures only one thing: How well Bastet thinks of you. The more you do for cats, the higher your Status.<br /> <br /> O: One moment you're an ordinary person, the next a Goddess has noticed you personally, even if only subconsciously. She has seen your works and judged them good. You gain a dot in the Mantle of Bastet, and an additional dot in Mantle for every dot of Status (maximum of five).<br /> <br /> OOO: At this level there is no benefit other than the increased Mantle, one of the drawbacks of not actually being an organisation.<br /> <br /> OOOOO: Bastet loves you so much that you gain some measure of cat like nature, a goddess warps the world with her attention alone: You can see in the dark, and gain 9again on perception rolls. You also get 9again on any athletics rolls and halve damage from a fall.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Kindnesses</span><br /> <br /> Bastet rewards those who show love to cats. There's so many ways to show love that her blessings fall upon many different people.<br /> <br /> The most common people who receive Bastet's blessings have adopted cats into their <b>Family</b>. They play with them, love them, and pet them for hours on end. Family can be anyone, from young girls who sleep with a cat wrapped around their feet to old women with one last companion left among the living.<br /> <br /> Free Speciality: Animal Ken (Felines)<br /> <br /> <b>Veterinarians </b>are blessed for their hard work and dedication. They underwent years of education and training to master the skills they needed to help cats. Most work as vets, healing the sick and carefully nursing injured cats back to health. Others might be zoo keepers, own a pet shop or simply provide a home and food to dozens of stray cats.<br /> <br /> Free Speciality: Medicine (Felines)<br /> <br /> The rarest of Bastet's Beloved are almost as <b>Feral </b>as the cat's they adore. Among their number can be found rangers, explorers, hunters and even feral children who were raised by cats. They have won the respect of wild and dangerous cats, and that won them Bastet's respect.<br /> <br /> Free Speciality: Survival (Felines)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Endowment: Mantle of Bastet (O \u2013 OOOOO)</span><br /> <br /> Bastet wasn't worshipped because she's cute and cuddly. The Ancient Egyptians held cats to be sacred because they dealt with vermin. They kept mice and rats from the fields and even hunted snakes.<br /> <br /> Bastet's Beloved rarely have to worry about vermin, not mice or... shall we say, vampires. When a cat judges a monster to be a serious threat to one of Bastet's Beloved (remember, cats are terrible gossips) the power of Bastet descends upon it. It's Strength and the damage rating for it's teeth and claws increase by Mantle. In additionally it's Size is treated as though it were Mantle points larger, both when calculating health and for other things like how hard it is to pick up or how heavy it is when it pounces upon a werewolf\u2019s back. However it's physical size does not change.<br /> <br /> The usual rules for temporary health do not apply. Instead place the additional boxes to the left of the health track, when the blessing fades any damage in those boxes is miraculously removed.<br /> <br /> The Mantle also has it's uses outside of battle. It is added to all Social rolls involving cats and even a single dot grants the ability to talk to cats in a human like manner. In addition no cat will ever attack anyone with the Mantle of Bastet. A lioness might forcefully push the Beloved away from her cubs, or a lion might challenge a Beloved for control of the pride or to a friendly wrestling bout, but they will do so with their claws retracted. Exceptional circumstances such as mind control or aggression inducing brain damage (such as rabies) might require the cat to roll to resist hurting Bastet's Beloved. Cats add Mantle to those rolls, and to resist being dissuaded from their holy duties. Unprovoked aggression against a cat breaks this protection (if your character does attack cats, expect to justify to the storyteller how on earth she has a Mantle)<br /> <br /> The Mantle of Bastet exists in a strange quantum state of being both a supernatural ability and not a supernatural ability. As a Goddess Bastet\u2019s more subtle influences aren\u2019t supernatural so much as changing what is \u201cnatural\u201d. Near one of her Beloved cat\u2019s just are naturally strong enough to fight monsters, but it still looks weird to humans. Generally though, when a mechanic affects supernatural beings or supernatural powers, Bastet\u2019s Beloved and their cats count as normal humans and the Mantel as a non-supernatural ability. Some powers are exception; for example they do trigger Unseen Senses keyed to the divine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-15-2021, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T09:55:50-07:00","id":632439,"title":"","content":"To everyone who was confused about just why <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/630251-at-long-last-i-m-writing-them\">LostLight was so excited</a> about a picture of a young girl holding a cat, here's what it signified.<br /> <br /> Back when Hunter: Mortal Remains was called Hunter: Monstrous Bastards I made a comment along the lines of &quot;It's called Hunter: Monstrous Bastards not Hunter: Kitten Cuddles&quot;. I've completely forgotten the context of that comment but it took a life of it's own. I made a joke thread outlining a book Hunter: Kitten Cuddles. Then I decided it wasn't silly enough (it was basically a book on the non-Vigil side of hunter's lives) and tried again in a second thread presenting a lighter and fluffier hunter - one of the compacts was a babysitter's club for monsters and the &quot;Conspiracy&quot; of Kitten Cuddles was Bastet's Beloved.<br /> <br /> That joke group was surprisingly well received and remembered. Two years later and LostLight brought it up as soon as the words &quot;talking cat&quot; were mentioned in a hunter context. Thus I decided it was time to dig out my old notes and finish them of.<br /> <br /> <br /> The crazy cat lady in the sample hunters is, I think, the single most fun I had writing for Hunter. And that includes the time I made TF:V responsible for Disney Faeries. BTW The Hakolel stereotype is a reference to <a href=\"https://youtu.be/wk6IB_Kgl4E?t=16s\" target=\"_blank\">The Rabbi's Cat</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-19-2020, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T04:20:22-07:00","id":633326,"title":"","content":"aaand added to my headcanon :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T09:43:53-07:00","id":633527,"title":"","content":"Pretty good work here, Kings Raven. It is pretty funny the way the cats go after that vampire. He really didn't see it coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T01:44:52-07:00","id":634376,"title":"","content":"Lol... good work indeed. It makes me wonder if there could be a more serious approach to it, after all isn't it a Stephen King story about cats hating specific type of monster and dealing with it? Than again, I am a cat lover, and still somewhat fondly remember playing an oWoD werecat in a Mage game where I was in catform for two full 4-hour sessions and still having a blast and being useful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T06:42:08-07:00","id":634547,"title":"","content":"This is a pretty weird, cool thing you made, Kings Raven.<br /> <br /> Not sure I follow why the Mantle doesn't count as a supernatural ability, but eh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T11:59:09-07:00","id":634919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/632408-convention-bastet-s-beloved-the-kitten-cuddlers?p=634547#post634547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure I follow why the Mantle doesn't count as a supernatural ability, but eh.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's to emphasise how deeply engrained into the fabric of reality Bastet is. The Mantle is part of every Cat like the Lie is part of every human. You can't just use Mind to remove the Lie from people's head, and you can't just use Life to remove the bonus Strength from Mantle.<br /> <br /> [edit] You can still cast spells that penalise strength on top of the mantle obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-22-2015, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T08:34:24-07:00","id":635825,"title":"","content":"It kind of reads like the Mantle is something that emanates from Bastet's Beloved rather than an inherent blessing of cats, so I can't say the write-up achieves that portrayal. To me at least.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of things deeply ingrained into the fabric of the World Of Darkness considered &quot;supernatural&quot; nonetheless, and supernal magic can indeed clear the Lie in mundane subjects and push the scales to fall from their eyes. It just isn't necessarily done with Mind because that is not in its purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T14:47:46-07:00","id":636284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/632408-convention-bastet-s-beloved-the-kitten-cuddlers?p=635825#post635825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It kind of reads like the Mantle is something that emanates from Bastet's Beloved rather than an inherent blessing of cats, so I can't say the write-up achieves that portrayal. To me at least.</div> </div> </div> </div> Technically that's correct. I was imprecise in my last post for reasons of brevity - I didn't think I needed to explain the entire complex interlocking systems that make up the Endowment to make the point that this is &quot;like the Lie&quot;.<br /> <br /> There are in fact two magical effects in play here. The Mantle is a magical blessing given to Bastet's Beloved. It grants the ability to talk to cats and emanates an aura. Cats exposed to this aura become favourably disposed to the Beloved (calling this &quot;mind control&quot; would be like saying your digestive system mind controls you to seek food when you're hungry) and can transmit the aura to other cats through all cat to cat methods of communication.<br /> <br /> The second effect is that in the World of Darkness every cat has the innate ability to gain super-strength, super-toughness and super-weight. However they can only unlock that ability when primed to do so by the Mantle's aura. It's a bit like those stories of parents lifting cars of their children, any human can achieve super-strength but only in extreme situations. In my WoD that ability to lift cars is also a supernatural ability provided by one or more parenting gods.<br /> <br /> Also. The Mantle is inherent to every human. In other words all humans have &quot;the inherent ability to develop The Mantle of Bastet through suffient kindness to cats&quot;. Bastet isn't sitting in Netjer-heven thinking &quot;who deserves a mantle this week&quot;. The simple fact that she exists bestows inherent traits upon both humans and cats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/632408-convention-bastet-s-beloved-the-kitten-cuddlers?p=635825#post635825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are plenty of things deeply ingrained into the fabric of the World Of Darkness considered &quot;supernatural&quot; nonetheless</div> </div> </div> </div> Such as? The only thing I can think of that engraned into the fabric of reality is the Lie and Fate.<br /> <br /> While you could muck about with someone's Fate you need Fate Arcana to do it. A general purpose anti-supernatural ability like Prime dispilation would not remove something like the Destiny Merit or Changeling's Fatebound Merits, or make non-merit prophecies about the target less likely to come true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/632408-convention-bastet-s-beloved-the-kitten-cuddlers?p=635825#post635825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and supernal magic can indeed clear the Lie in mundane subjects and push the scales to fall from their eyes. It just isn't necessarily done with Mind because that is not in its purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. I must have missed that preview. But the important point is that The Lie is an inherant property of (most) humans just like the Mantle<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T15:07:16-07:00","id":636298,"title":"","content":"I'd argue those inherent traits bestowed by Bastet are still supernatural ones at the end of the day, the same way the Lie is a supernatural facet of the World Of Darkness and occult physics are a supernatural facet of the World Of Darkness, and Fate (Mage, Changeling or Mummy) is a supernatural facet of the World Of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Saying the Mantle is inherent in the same way as the Lie is erronous, because the Lie is in every human from the start and the Mantle is something they can gain, making it no more inherent than a human's ability to learn Benedictions, to Awaken, or undergo the First Change. Likewise, saying that every cat has the innate ability to gain the blessings of the Mantle is really no different. Being inherent does not change its nature as part of the &quot;supernatural&quot;. And if it's a magical blessing then it's supernatural, simple.<br /> <br /> Soooo... sorry, I really don't see the point of the distinction or what it adds to the write-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-22-2015, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T01:36:49-07:00","id":636809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/632408-convention-bastet-s-beloved-the-kitten-cuddlers?p=636298#post636298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue those inherent traits bestowed by Bastet are still supernatural ones at the end of the day, the same way the Lie is a supernatural facet of the World Of Darkness and occult physics are a supernatural facet of the World Of Darkness, and Fate (Mage, Changeling or Mummy) is a supernatural facet of the World Of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you want to call the Lie supernatural than be my guest. However that doesn't change the fact that despite having a shard of the Abyss in their soul and the power to unravel Supernal magic WoD mortals are still considered to be non-supernatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/632408-convention-bastet-s-beloved-the-kitten-cuddlers?p=636298#post636298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying the Mantle is inherent in the same way as the Lie is erronous, because the Lie is in every human from the start and the Mantle is something they can gain, making it no more inherent than a human's ability to learn Benedictions, to Awaken, or undergo the First Change.</div> </div> </div> </div> This logic doesn't work. Language is inherent to all humans but it's not present from the start.<br /> <br /> All humans have the ability to develop language skills if exposed to language at an early age. In my WoD all humans have the ability to develop a cat affecting aura if they're kind enough to cats. Both are innate parts of humanity that happen automatically if exposed to a certain stimulus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/632408-convention-bastet-s-beloved-the-kitten-cuddlers?p=636298#post636298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo... sorry, I really don't see the point of the distinction or what it adds to the write-up.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are mechanics that work differently depending on if you're supernatural or natural. Bastet's Beloved are harder to detect and harder to protect against.<br /> <br /> Plus the setting is more interesting if your blur the division between natural and supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-23-2015, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T02:00:27-07:00","id":636818,"title":"","content":"just my two cents on the matter and how I see things, but I think that the Mantle does not considered as a supernatural ability because it is not about calling down the power of the saints, awakening your demonic blood or drinking mystical potions- it is about being a cat. It allows you to speak with cats, making cats more powerful and do all the other things it does about cats. The point is that every person can become a crazy cat person, it just needs to be awakened by the goddess- which is why you don't need to learn that Endowment through a real organization. That's the most fun part of the group- everyone are potential Beloved (unless you are a dog person, and than you join Fenrir's Bastards, and no one likes those guys :P).<br /> <br /> In sort, the point is that being Beloved by cats is something natural, something which everyone could do without having to learn it. It is an instinctive ability which most of the people who possess it doesn't even know they have it (sure, they speak with cats and those cats can tackle down werewolves, but whatever). It is not a miracle or sorcery or an high tech item- it is just something those who really, truly love cats can do, and Bastet, being a cat, was to one to allow that thing to exist. Also, it is more funny that way :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T05:08:04-07:00","id":636892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/632408-convention-bastet-s-beloved-the-kitten-cuddlers?p=636809#post636809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This logic doesn't work. Language is inherent to all humans but it's not present from the start.<br /> <br /> All humans have the ability to develop language skills if exposed to language at an early age. In my WoD all humans have the ability to develop a cat affecting aura if they're kind enough to cats. Both are innate parts of humanity that happen automatically if exposed to a certain stimulus.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, exactly <i>as</i> innate as the ability to learn Benedictions, or the capacity to Awaken? The logic stands, you're just not being coherent.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to tell you how your version of the WoD should work, but following the logic of the 'canon'* WoD presented to us, the Mantle as written is not at all like the Lie. So I find the original point of contention a flaw in the write-up of Bastet's Beloved, I'm afraid.<br /> <br /> The mental image of a cat tackling a werewolf to the ground is still hilarious though, and I don't disagree that blurring apparently clear-cut divisions can make things more interesting.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*Quoted because, well, canon is in many cases ultimately the decision of the Storyteller and the group, rather than something enforced by the books.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-23-2015, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T06:29:46-07:00","id":636929,"title":"","content":"No, because Benedictions do not happen automatically if you're exposed to the vatican library. If you don't see how language is innate to humanity in a way that, for example, learning calculus isn't then I don't think we can find agreement.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T07:42:13-07:00","id":637005,"title":"","content":"&quot;Language does not happen automatically if you're exposed to people who can use it, but aren't actually demonstrating it.&quot;<br /> <br /> We aren't born with knowledge of complex communication. Neither are we born with knowledge of calculus.<br /> <br /> In other words, yes, in the context of this discussion we disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T10:14:04-07:00","id":639267,"title":"","content":"You know this whole Mantle thingy being all quantum and stuff makes a good bypass to it being &quot;magic&quot;. I kinda like to think of the Wyrd the same way. Sorry about the outta place reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T10:24:26-07:00","id":639272,"title":"","content":"Well I wouldn't call the Wyrd out of place <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I think that most of what people call Fate is the Wyrd and Fate's already cropped up in this discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}